version: 2.0.0
description: >-
  Ratified design specifications. Each spec is the buildable contract for a
  feature; Builder implements it verbatim, and amendments append rather than
  rewrite history. Examples: gnomon.md (the Paradigm 8.0 kernel),
  cid-captain-agent.md, brain.md, classroom.md, agent-adoption.md. The Warpline
  specs (warpline-code-lens.md, warpline-fabric-schema-v2.md,
  warpline-v1-anchor.md, warpline-v3-identity.md) form the VCS trust-floor
  lineage. Markdown only, no code.
context:
  - "Warpline spec lineage registered by Arky (T-2026-07-03-003): fabric-schema-v2 → v1-anchor → v3-identity"
  - "warpline-forge.md (T-2026-07-14-005) is a DRAFT CONSTRAINT spec, not a build contract — SPEC-ONLY, no forge code until graded-weaves/week > 0; it constrains Phase-2 API shapes (verdict JSON, KNOT payload, claim schema, injection envelope)"
  - "warpline-v1-anchor.md: v1-prefix epoch anchor (backfill → attest-once → freeze; closes HIGH-A/HIGH-B/MED-C). warpline-v3-identity.md: v3 position-free DAG identity, designed before M2 branching and built later."
